  "reason": "One canary dispatch of a unit at rest, per reference shape and state. The counts are the dispatch's own work: the live reads hand out the stored pods themselves in a fresh list and the replica and the service by copy, the cached reads hand out copies; the bytes carry the pod list the pass is handed (one entry per pod) and the rows it decodes. live-gets are the replica reads through the live reader, one per member per pass: the observation of its rows keeps the replica as read, and the Services sweep and the rollback signal work from that object instead of reading the member again; live-service-gets the read of the service's record before the rollback signal, one per pass; live-lists the pod lists through the live reader, one per member; pods-listed the pods they hand out; cache-reads the Service and ControllerRevision reads; cache-pod-lists the pod lists through the cache, cache-pods-listed the pods they hand out and cache-pods-copied the pods they copy, none while the dispatch lists pods live; live-json the allocations and bytes of the pass with every live read decoded from the JSON the apiserver serves, which is what the manager pays for them: the pod list is about fifty allocations and 4 to 6 KB per pod of it. The two prefill/decode holding rows move by a few allocations between recordings. A pass at rest writes nothing and changes no pod.",
